<xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" elementFormDefault="qualified"><xs:annotation><xs:documentation>
      Operome: OperomeStGBLiberty
      Source: StGB consolidated, offences against personal liberty (provenance StGB 232, 232a, 232b, 233, 233a, 234, 235, 236, 237, 239, 239a, 239b, 240, 241; German governs)
      One combined carrier for the fourteen sections of the Eighteenth Title. Each section is a SectionScope;
      identifiers resolve within their SectionScope. The same token (for example Person, Exploits, Violence,
      ThreatOfSeriousHarm, Seizes) may carry a section-specific surface form: each section's variables are declared in
      that section's own groups, exactly as emitted by the per-section build, and the per-section schemas remain the
      canonical single-section substrates. The 232 scope authors the exploitative-employment definition consumed by
      name in 232b, 233 and 233a; the 239 scope authors the deprivation pair consumed by 233a. Objective Tatbestand
      only; purpose and knowledge elements retained where the markup retains them; penalty excluded; silent repairs
      against the German recorded in the Flags annexes of the working document, not here.
    </xs:documentation><xs:appinfo><PackageMeta><Subject>StGB Consolidated, Offences Against Personal Liberty (§232 to §241)</Subject><Verb>commit</Verb><Article>StGB 232, 232a, 232b, 233, 233a, 234, 235, 236, 237, 239, 239a, 239b, 240, 241</Article><ShortName>OperomeStGBLiberty</ShortName></PackageMeta></xs:appinfo></xs:annotation><xs:simpleType name="TristateEnum"><xs:restriction base="xs:string"><xs:enumeration value="true"/><xs:enumeration value="false"/><xs:enumeration value="unknown"/></xs:restriction></xs:simpleType>

